  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "While working on a world with a large VRCUrl array, I noticed VRChat's memory usage ballooned quickly upon rejoining the world multiple times.\n\nI've put together a test world that shows this behavior. To make the behavior more apparent, it contains an unrealistic 2 million+ URLs that are each 64 characters long: https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_9029bdaf-6d58-4b3d-8c1e-ad6c8d4149e5\n\nUpon joining this world immediately after starting VRChat, VRChat's memory usage is ~3.8GiB. Upon subsequent rejoins, it quickly approaches ~6.7GiB, and hovers around there for several rejoins before jumping to ~7.2GiB, ~7.7GiB, etc.\n\nI rejoined enough times to hit ~8.6GiB.\n\nI'm hesitant to call this a memory leak as it could just be heap/garbage collection related, but the RAM usage stays high even when leaving to go to a lighter world.\n\nIn general, I've found rejoining a \"normal\" world a dozen times in a row only sees a memory increase of a few dozen megabytes at most, so I still believe there is something odd going on here even if it's not a true memory leak.",
